// std.path_style: how the target spells a path (MYLA-704, D215), which
// std.path, std.fs and std.glob read: Linux's and WASI's here. A target
// whose paths differ has a copy of its own beside its platform module
// (`path_style_windows.my` beside `platform_windows.my`), which the loader
// takes for this one, as it takes `std/platform.my`'s (`for_target`). A
// module this small, so that knowing the target costs a check nothing:
// std.platform's constant made checking a program that imports std.path
// 26.2 M → 40.4 M instructions (2026-11-15, against 194c9dc).

// Whether `\` separates a path's components as `/` does, and a path may
// start with a drive or a UNC share before its root (Windows'): no.
pub const WINDOWS: bool = false
